message.content:
{
  "sample_id": "11968173_t1",
  "next_action_type": "CTNF",
  "claim_ground_evidence": [
    {
      "claim_ids": [
        14
      ],
      "ground": "103",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": [
        "GVNXDYBTPXXIFW1"
      ],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "Claim 14 as amended recites: (a) battery operated audio microchip system recording on multiple channels; (b) a single playback button which can operate each channel; (c) an LED corresponding to each channel that turns on when that channel has an active message; and (d) a means to turn each LED off. The Examiner's prior action relied on the Multi Message Recorder (MMR) to teach the LED-per-channel and related LED behavior, and on Pawlowski (US 6,038,199) to teach selecting among multiple stored messages and playback with a single control. Combining those teachings would have made the claimed device obvious to a person of ordinary skill in the art for the reasons stated below.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "GQO3GTZ0PPOPPY5",
          "support_span": "Claims 1-9, 11, and 13 are rejected under 35 U.S.C. 102(a) as being anticipated by “Multi Message Recorder” (MMR).",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
